\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{The equilibrium persists}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{In the Hopf column of \ref{fnip-0005}, each applied current has
one equilibrium. \citet{p. 56}{ermentrout2010mathematical} records
that this equilibrium is stable for #{I_{\mathrm{app}}<94} and
for #{I_{\mathrm{app}}>212}. At those two values a complex
conjugate pair of eigenvalues lies on the imaginary axis. The
equilibrium does not disappear. A periodic orbit branches from
it.}

\p{The periodic orbits near those values are unstable, and they
lie on the same side of each value as the stable equilibrium.
\citet{pp. 56–57}{ermentrout2010mathematical} names both changes
subcritical Hopf bifurcations. A supercritical Hopf bifurcation
has a stable periodic orbit on the side where the equilibrium
is unstable. \citet{§6.1.3, p. 169}{izhikevich2007dynamical}
uses the same division: the cubic coefficient is negative in
the supercritical case and positive in the subcritical case.}
